# item40/item40e: Amos01 route. Player input plus named use/grab of map actors; no teleport,
# set_goal, take_control or weapon grant. Input is ignored by the run while the authored
# cinematics own the controller (intro Cine0, Jones Cine3).
#
# item40e findings (local/reports/item40e-amos01-doorway.md):
#   - Porte14/15 on the office north wall are the sliding panels of a wall cupboard
#     (AMplacar01 + AMplacarport01) on a 384-UU-thick solid BSP wall: there is no doorway.
#   - The office's only player exit is the south door Porte17 (8,-528), a PlayerTriggerToggle
#     XIIIPorte opened by use; opening it fires its OpeningEvent dialamos3tempo.
#   - The ground-floor ducts are entered through breakable floor-level grilles
#     (XIDCine.BreakableMover, AMaeraplaq); the player starts without fists, so a deco pickup
#     (ChaiseDeco -> DecoChair, one swing) breaks a grille.
t=0.50 forward 1
t=1.50 forward 0
# Control returns after the intro (~t=84). Jones (Cine3) waits "wait player 192" behind the
# office vent grille: walk to him so his scene (jones03, exit through the vent duct) finishes.
t=86.00 goto 800 330
# Down the office stairs to the south door and open it.
t=100.00 goto 420 -470
t=104.00 goto 60 -300
t=108.00 goto 72 -470
t=110.00 yaw 270
t=110.50 use
# Corridor (zone 22) -> zone 25; grab the chair ChaiseDeco2 (Grab: bCanPickup branch).
t=114.00 goto 72 -700
t=118.00 goto 288 -1000
t=121.00 goto 156 -1053
t=122.50 track ChaiseDeco2
t=123.00 use ChaiseDeco2
t=123.10 track off
t=123.50 switch_weapon 20
# Break the duct grille BreakAbleMover16 with the chair swing.
t=125.00 goto 175 -1198
t=127.00 track BreakAbleMover16
t=128.00 shoot
t=129.50 track off
# Crouch and crawl the 128-UU duct (zone 26) west to its far grille BreakAbleMover17.
t=130.00 crouch on
t=130.50 goto 60 -1198
t=133.00 goto -300 -1198
t=137.00 goto -505 -1198
t=150.00 wait_travel
